cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use A2SP, please cite it using this metadata, together with the papers referenced in the README."
title: "A2SP: Asymmetric Two-Step Pairing framework toolkit"
version: v0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Qingquan
    affiliation: "Wuhan Textile University"
    email: qqtang@wtu.edu.cn
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the Asymmetric Two-Step Pairing (A2SP) framework:
  one pairing kernel, any domain. Every A2SP channel rate carries a common
  carrier factor that cancels exactly in the reduced trajectory equations
  dY/dX = -1 + kappa*Y/X (resonance line kappa = 1), leaving closed-form,
  fit-free laws. The kernel source is the unified theory of generalized
  step-growth polymerization; the first application is two-stage rumor
  spreading (Maki-Thompson). Includes two runnable examples (rumor model with
  network cascade; step-growth polymerization core), 53 regression tests
  (23 published-anchor), and stochastic engines (Gillespie well-mixed with pair
  self-correction; configuration-model network CTMC).
keywords:
  - A2SP
  - asymmetric two-step pairing
  - step-growth polymerization
  - kinetic asymmetry
  - rumour spreading
  - Maki-Thompson
  - exact solutions
license: MIT
